<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Beni Isguen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Beni Isguen is one of the five fortified towns of the Mzab valley in the Algerian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a>, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghardaia">Ghardaïa</a>. Considered the holiest of the five, it kept strict Ibadi rules, with gates closed at night and limited access for outsiders. Its walls, mosque and daily auction market are part of the M'zab Valley World Heritage Site.</p></div>
